  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 335 AM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nThe surface low moves into eastern Illinois by Saturday afternoon. \nCold advection on the west side of the low along with continuing \nshowers and clouds should produce a cool day with highs struggling \nto reach the upper 70s.  This will likely be the coolest day of the \nnext 7, although the latest model runs keep temperatures below \nnormal at least through Monday.  High pressure moves into the \nMidwest on Sunday as the short wave continues digging and amplifies \nthe long wave trough over the eastern U.S.  This should put an end \nto most of the precip, although some isolated showers remain \npossible Sunday afternoon over southern Illinois and southeast \nMissouri as moisture wraps around the western side of the low level \nwave over the lower Ohio Valley.  Medium range guidance shows the \nlong wave pattern shifting eastward through midweek with the upper \nlevel ridge stretching into the Mid Mississippi Valley. Temperatures \ngradually warm up, finally reaching the upper 80s to around 90 by \nWednesday. Dew point temperatures also rise gradually, and heat \nindex values could be back to around 100 degrees Wednesday afternoon.",
